{
  // AppSession — one row per end-user login on one device/browser. The client
  // heartbeat (src/lib/SessionHeartbeat.jsx) creates the row on login and moves
  // last_active_at every ~60s; ACACIA Mission Control reads these via the
  // acaciaControl bridge (sessions.list) to show "sesiones activas por usuario"
  // and sets revoked_at (sessions.revoke) to force a logout — the client checks
  // its own row each heartbeat and calls logout() when revoked.
  //
  // RLS: service role (role:admin) has full access so the bridge can list/revoke;
  // an end user only touches THEIR OWN rows, scoped by the built-in created_by_id
  // (Base44 sets it on create — cannot be spoofed by a forged data.user_id).
  //
  // Deferred (2026-10-05, Base44 scan fingerprint 203124ba, severity low,
  // verdict plausible): user_email/user_name are still free-form client input
  // on create (SessionHeartbeat.jsx), so a signed-in user can spoof another
  // member's name/email in Mission Control's "sesiones activas" panel. Locking
  // those two fields the way revoked_at/revoked_by are locked below isn't
  // enough on its own — they are `required`, so the client's direct
  // AppSession.create() would then need the server to supply them, which
  // means routing session-row creation through a backend function (deriving
  // user_email/user_name from auth.me(), mirroring markWelcomeShown's shape)
  // rather than a same-day entity-schema change. Flagged for whoever next
  // touches AppSession or SessionHeartbeat.jsx.
  "name": "AppSession",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "user_email": { "type": "string", "description": "Email del usuario de la sesión" },
    "user_name": { "type": "string", "description": "Nombre para mostrar" },
    "device": { "type": "string", "description": "Etiqueta corta del navegador/dispositivo (p.ej. 'Chrome · macOS')" },
    "started_at": { "type": "string", "format": "date-time", "description": "Inicio de sesión" },
    "last_active_at": { "type": "string", "format": "date-time", "description": "Última actividad (movida por el latido)" },
    "revoked_at": {
      "type": "string",
      "format": "date-time",
      "description": "Marcada por Mission Control para forzar el cierre de sesión. Bloqueado al service role: el RLS a nivel de entidad deja a cada usuario actualizar su propia fila entera, y sin este candado un cliente podía llamar AppSession.update(suPropioId, {revoked_at: null}) para des-revocarse y evadir el cierre forzado (hallazgo del scan de seguridad de Base44, 2026-10-05, fingerprint 203124ba).",
      "rls": {
        "write": {
          "user_condition": { "role": "admin" }
        }
      }
    },
    "revoked_by": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Operador que forzó el cierre (auditoría). Mismo candado que revoked_at: el cliente nunca debe poder escribir esta columna de auditoría.",
      "rls": {
        "write": {
          "user_condition": { "role": "admin" }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "required": ["user_email"],
  "rls": {
    "create": {
      "$or": [
        { "user_condition": { "role": "admin" } },
        { "created_by_id": "{{user.id}}" }
      ]
    },
    "read": {
      "$or": [
        { "user_condition": { "role": "admin" } },
        { "created_by_id": "{{user.id}}" }
      ]
    },
    "update": {
      "$or": [
        { "user_condition": { "role": "admin" } },
        { "created_by_id": "{{user.id}}" }
      ]
    },
    "delete": {
      "user_condition": { "role": "admin" }
    }
  }
}
